(from here on referred to as the "eWiz Source"), with the following restrictions:

- If you publish any work derived from the eWiz Source, you must make it apparent
  in some way that it is derived from the eWiz Source.

- If you have created an executable program (from here on called "Your Program")
  compiled from some source code and/or other source files (from here on called
  "Your Source"), and if Your Source includes files or source code copied or
  derived from the eWiz Source, then you may only publish Your Program under the
  following conditions:

    - Your Program does not contain any malware or hidden malicious content.

    - You may not charge users money for Your Program, and Your Source must
      contain the monetization systems present in the eWiz Source, including the
      licensing, trial-period tracking, and payment systems, without any
      alterations, and all of these systems must be active and working as
      intended in Your Program, paying the original author. That is unless Your
      Source features substantial improvements or additions to the eWiz Source,
      such that Your Source should be considered its own, derivative work,
      separate from the eWiz Source.

    - You may not publish Your Program under the name "eWiz", or under a name or
      with an icon so similar that users could mistake it for eWiz.

