# Notes on the eWiz License

The eWiz License has two goals:

1. To stop people with bad intentions, or people out for a quick buck, from
   publishing apps based on eWiz: an app that looks like eWiz but carries malware,
   or an app that is eWiz except that when you buy a license someone other than
   the author gets paid.

2. To let everyone else do anything they like with the eWiz source code: reuse it
   in their own free or paid projects, write bug fixes and improvements to eWiz and
   publish them, or make a substantial improvement to eWiz and charge for that
   improved version or release it for free.

The license is meant to be open source in spirit, with protections against bad
actors now that eWiz is a paid app. Note that there are no restrictions at all on
how you use the source code, only on publishing apps compiled from it.

eWiz is "source-available", not open source by the OSI definition, because of the
publishing restrictions above.

The in-app purchase buys a license key for the eWiz app; it does not change these
terms, which govern the source code.
